cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ferrofluid Topology: structured-light 3D reconstruction of the Rosensweig instability"
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Prineas
    given-names: John
repository-code: "https://github.com/johnprineas/ferrofluid-topology"
abstract: >-
  A fringe-projection profilometry pipeline for measuring the surface topology of
  magnetised ferrofluid. Camera intrinsics are recovered as Brown-Conrady distortion
  coefficients from a projected checkerboard; projector extrinsics from asymmetric
  circle-grid detection and solvePnP, validated against synthetic keystone homographies
  at known pitch, yaw and roll. Fringe centrelines are extracted by sub-pixel Gaussian
  peak fitting, indexed by phase unwrapping and triangulated to a height field. Used to
  measure the Rosensweig critical wavelength as 8.3 +/- 0.4 mm at 10.6 mT against a
  7.6-9.8 mm ferrohydrodynamic continuum prediction.
keywords:
  - ferrofluid
  - Rosensweig instability
  - structured light
  - fringe projection profilometry
  - camera calibration
  - computer vision
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-06-30"
